  "narrative": {
    "story": "Rolex revived the Milgauss in 2007 and gave the GV version a green-tinted sapphire crystal — 'Glace Verte' — over a black, and from 2014 an electric 'Z-Blue', dial with the orange lightning-bolt seconds hand. The antimagnetic shield and caliber 3131 continued the 1950s scientist's-watch brief. When Rolex dropped the Milgauss entirely in 2023, the GV became the line's closing statement and secondary interest picked up.",
